1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,190
Almost four hundred years ago,

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:07,290
a scientist called Jan van Helmont
planted a small willow tree in a pot of

3
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:08,520
dried soil.

4
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:10,380
He weighed the tree.

5
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,240
He weighed the soil.

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,080
Then, for five years,

7
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,640
he gave it nothing but
water. The tree grew.

8
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:22,910
It gained about seventy-four
kilograms. And the soil?

9
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:26,140
It had lost only about
fifty-seven grams.

10
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:32,800
So where did a whole tree's worth
of mass come from? Not the soil.

11
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,110
Most of the wood came
out of thin air.

12
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,540
By the end of this video,

13
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,290
you'll know exactly how,

14
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,260
and how to explain it in an exam.

15
00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:50,180
You eat to get your
food. Plants don't.

16
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,220
Plants make their own food,

17
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,900
by photosynthesis.

18
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:57,580
Here's the definition
the mark scheme wants.

19
00:00:57,580 --> 00:00:59,980
Learn it word for word.

20
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:04,340
Photosynthesis is the process by
which plants synthesise carbohydrates

21
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,720
from raw materials
using energy from light.

22
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:10,530
Let's break that down.

23
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,400
Synthesise means make.

24
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:15,030
The carbohydrate it makes is glucose,

25
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:16,550
a simple sugar.

26
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:20,120
The raw materials are
carbon dioxide and water.

27
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:23,580
And the energy to do
it comes from light.

28
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:26,490
Now the word equation.

29
00:01:26,490 --> 00:01:28,630
Carbon dioxide, plus water,

30
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:31,130
gives glucose, plus oxygen.

31
00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:35,370
And it happens in the presence
of light and chlorophyll,

32
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:38,050
so we write those on the arrow.

33
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:40,750
They're conditions, not reactants.

34
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:42,500
Light isn't a substance,

35
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,000
and chlorophyll isn't used up.

36
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,720
So where do the raw
materials come from?

37
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:52,580
Carbon dioxide diffuses
into the leaf from the air.

38
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:55,880
Water is absorbed from
the soil by the roots,

39
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:57,770
and travels up the stem,

40
00:01:57,770 --> 00:02:00,400
in the xylem, to the leaf.

41
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,950
Oxygen is a waste product.

42
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:06,060
Some is used in the
plant's own respiration,

43
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:10,440
and the rest diffuses out
of the leaf, into the air.

44
00:02:11,390 --> 00:02:15,550
You also need to know the
balanced symbol equation.

45
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:18,890
Six C O two, plus six H two O,

46
00:02:18,890 --> 00:02:21,560
gives C six H twelve O six,

47
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,420
plus six O two.

48
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,930
Let's check it balances.

49
00:02:25,930 --> 00:02:28,090
Carbon: six on the left,

50
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:29,800
six on the right.

51
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,520
Hydrogen: twelve on each side.

52
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:36,390
Oxygen: twelve plus six
makes eighteen on the left,

53
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:41,480
and six plus twelve makes eighteen
on the right. It balances.

54
00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:45,950
So, what does the light actually do?

55
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:49,370
Inside the cells of a
leaf are chloroplasts.

56
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:51,530
Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll,

57
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:53,400
a green pigment.

58
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,470
Chlorophyll absorbs light.

59
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:59,660
Then it transfers energy from
light into energy in chemicals,

60
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:02,360
for the synthesis of carbohydrates.

61
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:06,750
In other words, that energy
ends up stored in glucose.

62
00:03:07,250 --> 00:03:09,990
Be careful with your wording here.

63
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:13,130
Never write that
chlorophyll makes energy.

64
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:14,990
Energy can't be made.

65
00:03:14,990 --> 00:03:17,010
Chlorophyll transfers it.

66
00:03:17,010 --> 00:03:20,220
So use the syllabus word: transfers.

67
00:03:21,170 --> 00:03:23,710
So the plant has made glucose.

68
00:03:23,710 --> 00:03:25,520
What happens to it?

69
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,110
There are five uses to learn.

70
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:31,440
One. Glucose is used in respiration,

71
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:34,520
to release energy for
the plant's cells.

72
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,500
Two. Glucose is turned into starch,

73
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,310
as an energy store.

74
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:40,820
Starch is insoluble,

75
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:45,360
so storing it doesn't affect the
movement of water by osmosis.

76
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:48,730
Three. Glucose is used
to make cellulose,

77
00:03:48,730 --> 00:03:51,080
which builds the cell walls.

78
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:55,590
Four. Glucose is changed
into sucrose, another sugar.

79
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:58,220
Sucrose is transported in the phloem,

80
00:03:58,220 --> 00:04:01,790
to other parts of
the plant. And five.

81
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:04,120
Sugars are used to make nectar,

82
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:07,890
in flowers, to attract
insects for pollination.

83
00:04:08,390 --> 00:04:10,520
Respiration. Starch.

84
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:13,640
Cellulose. Sucrose. Nectar.

85
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:16,930
But glucose only contains carbon,

86
00:04:16,930 --> 00:04:18,700
hydrogen and oxygen.

87
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:21,610
To grow, a plant also needs proteins,

88
00:04:21,610 --> 00:04:24,690
and proteins are made
from amino acids.

89
00:04:24,690 --> 00:04:27,300
Amino acids contain nitrogen.

90
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:30,460
So plants absorb nitrate
ions from the soil,

91
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:32,230
through their roots.

92
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:35,650
Nitrate ions are needed
to make amino acids.

93
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,310
Without enough nitrate,

94
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:39,450
the plant has stunted growth,

95
00:04:39,450 --> 00:04:42,240
and its older leaves turn yellow.

96
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:45,390
Plants also absorb magnesium ions.

97
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:48,820
Magnesium ions are needed
to make chlorophyll.

98
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:50,580
Without enough magnesium,

99
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:53,760
the leaves turn yellow
between the veins.

100
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:56,930
Less chlorophyll means
less light is absorbed,

101
00:04:56,930 --> 00:04:59,390
so there's less photosynthesis.

102
00:04:59,890 --> 00:05:02,440
In an exam, link three things:

103
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:05,050
the ion, what it's used to make,

104
00:05:05,050 --> 00:05:07,500
and what happens without it.

105
00:05:08,450 --> 00:05:11,330
Most photosynthesis
happens in the leaves,

106
00:05:11,330 --> 00:05:14,170
and leaves are adapted for it.

107
00:05:14,170 --> 00:05:16,760
Most leaves are broad and thin.

108
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:19,190
Broad means a large surface area,

109
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:21,100
to absorb more light.

110
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:25,820
Thin means a short distance for carbon
dioxide to diffuse to the cells

111
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:26,860
inside.

112
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:29,650
Now let's cut a leaf open.

113
00:05:29,650 --> 00:05:34,440
This is a cross-section through
the leaf of a dicotyledonous plant.

114
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:38,100
That's a plant whose seeds
have two seed leaves.

115
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:40,510
It's a simplified diagram.

116
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:43,800
For each part, you
need to know its name,

117
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:46,350
and how it helps photosynthesis.

118
00:05:46,350 --> 00:05:50,440
Let's go through it layer
by layer, from the top.

119
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:53,190
First, the waxy cuticle.

120
00:05:53,190 --> 00:05:54,890
It reduces water loss,

121
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:56,890
and because it's transparent,

122
00:05:56,890 --> 00:05:59,790
light passes straight through it.

123
00:05:59,790 --> 00:06:02,140
Next, the upper epidermis.

124
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:04,430
These cells are transparent too,

125
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:06,620
and they have no chloroplasts,

126
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:10,290
so light passes through
to the cells below.

127
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:12,550
Then the palisade mesophyll.

128
00:06:12,550 --> 00:06:14,200
These cells are tall,

129
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:17,310
tightly packed, close
to the top surface,

130
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:19,420
and full of chloroplasts.

131
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,960
So they absorb the most light.

132
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:25,200
This is where most
photosynthesis happens.

133
00:06:26,150 --> 00:06:29,430
Below the palisade is
the spongy mesophyll.

134
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:31,130
Its cells are rounder,

135
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:32,590
and loosely packed,

136
00:06:32,590 --> 00:06:34,990
with air spaces between them.

137
00:06:34,990 --> 00:06:38,880
The air spaces let carbon
dioxide diffuse to the cells,

138
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:42,980
and they give a large surface
area for gas exchange.

139
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:46,910
Running through the leaf
are vascular bundles.

140
00:06:46,910 --> 00:06:51,010
The xylem brings water and
mineral ions into the leaf.

141
00:06:51,010 --> 00:06:54,370
The phloem carries sucrose
and amino acids away,

142
00:06:54,370 --> 00:06:56,760
to the rest of the plant.

143
00:06:57,260 --> 00:07:00,130
On the underside is
the lower epidermis,

144
00:07:00,130 --> 00:07:02,630
with tiny pores called stomata.

145
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:05,020
One pore is called a stoma.

146
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:08,240
Carbon dioxide diffuses
in through the stomata,

147
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,300
and oxygen diffuses out.

148
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:14,730
Each stoma is opened and closed
by a pair of guard cells.

149
00:07:14,730 --> 00:07:17,590
In the light, they open the stomata,

150
00:07:17,590 --> 00:07:20,380
so carbon dioxide can diffuse in.

151
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,990
So, from top to bottom:

152
00:07:22,990 --> 00:07:24,940
cuticle, upper epidermis,

153
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:26,310
palisade mesophyll,

154
00:07:26,310 --> 00:07:28,800
spongy mesophyll, vascular bundle,

155
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:32,280
lower epidermis with
stomata and guard cells.

156
00:07:33,430 --> 00:07:37,870
So how can you show that a leaf
has been photosynthesising?

157
00:07:37,870 --> 00:07:39,420
Test it for starch,

158
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:43,520
because a leaf stores some
of its glucose as starch.

159
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:46,370
First, destarch the plant.

160
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:49,570
Put it in the dark for a day or two.

161
00:07:49,570 --> 00:07:52,490
With no light, it
can't photosynthesise,

162
00:07:52,490 --> 00:07:55,220
so it uses up its stored starch.

163
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:59,840
That means any starch you find later
must have been made during your

164
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:02,530
experiment. Step one:

165
00:08:02,530 --> 00:08:06,380
put the leaf in boiling
water for about a minute.

166
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:08,030
This kills the cells,

167
00:08:08,030 --> 00:08:10,560
and breaks down the cell membranes,

168
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:14,590
so the iodine can get
in later. Step two:

169
00:08:14,590 --> 00:08:16,890
turn off the Bunsen burner.

170
00:08:16,890 --> 00:08:20,380
Then put the leaf in a
boiling tube of ethanol,

171
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:23,010
and stand it in the hot water.

172
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:24,570
Ethanol is flammable,

173
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:27,590
so never heat it with a naked flame.

174
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:30,370
The hot ethanol removes
the chlorophyll,

175
00:08:30,370 --> 00:08:35,180
so the colour change will
be easy to see. Step three:

176
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:37,570
dip the leaf in warm water.

177
00:08:37,570 --> 00:08:39,710
The ethanol makes it brittle,

178
00:08:39,710 --> 00:08:43,310
and the water softens it. Step four:

179
00:08:43,310 --> 00:08:45,780
spread the leaf on a white tile,

180
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:48,100
so the colour is easy to see,

181
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:50,260
and add iodine solution.

182
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:52,260
If it turns blue-black,

183
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:53,930
starch is present.

184
00:08:53,930 --> 00:08:55,730
If it stays orange-brown,

185
00:08:55,730 --> 00:08:57,450
there's no starch.

186
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:03,090
Now you can use that test to
show what photosynthesis needs.

187
00:09:03,090 --> 00:09:05,640
Each experiment needs a control.

188
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:08,260
A control is identical to the test,

189
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:11,690
except for the one factor
you're investigating.

190
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:15,740
It shows that the result
was caused by that factor.

191
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:18,060
First, chlorophyll.

192
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:21,360
Take a destarched plant
with variegated leaves:

193
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:24,880
leaves that are partly
green and partly white.

194
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:27,720
The white parts have no chlorophyll.

195
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:30,670
Leave it in the light
for a few hours,

196
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:32,380
then test a leaf.

197
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:35,220
Only the green parts turn blue-black.

198
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,820
The white parts stay orange-brown.

199
00:09:37,820 --> 00:09:40,460
The green parts are the control.

200
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:42,670
So chlorophyll is needed.

201
00:09:43,170 --> 00:09:44,740
Second, light.

202
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:46,540
Take a destarched plant,

203
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:50,050
and cover part of one
leaf with black paper.

204
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:53,260
Leave it in the light
for a few hours.

205
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:57,560
After the test, only the
uncovered part turns blue-black.

206
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:00,300
The uncovered part is the control.

207
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:02,210
So light is needed.

208
00:10:02,710 --> 00:10:04,770
Third, carbon dioxide.

209
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:06,570
Take a destarched plant,

210
00:10:06,570 --> 00:10:08,070
and seal one leaf,

211
00:10:08,070 --> 00:10:11,520
still attached, inside
a flask with soda lime,

212
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:13,830
which absorbs carbon dioxide.

213
00:10:13,830 --> 00:10:16,310
The control is an identical flask,

214
00:10:16,310 --> 00:10:18,070
with no soda lime.

215
00:10:18,070 --> 00:10:20,490
After a few hours in the light,

216
00:10:20,490 --> 00:10:23,430
only the control leaf
turns blue-black.

217
00:10:23,430 --> 00:10:25,880
So carbon dioxide is needed.

218
00:10:27,030 --> 00:10:30,490
Next: how fast is
photosynthesis happening?

219
00:10:30,490 --> 00:10:32,010
That's its rate.

220
00:10:32,010 --> 00:10:35,760
To measure it, use
pondweed, a water plant.

221
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:39,560
Put it in water with a little
sodium hydrogencarbonate,

222
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:41,920
which supplies carbon dioxide.

223
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:47,330
In the light, the pondweed gives
off bubbles of gas, mostly oxygen.

224
00:10:47,630 --> 00:10:50,030
Count the bubbles per minute.

225
00:10:50,030 --> 00:10:52,410
Or, for more accurate results,

226
00:10:52,410 --> 00:10:55,230
collect the gas and
measure its volume,

227
00:10:55,230 --> 00:10:58,320
because bubbles can
be different sizes.

228
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:01,010
To change the light intensity,

229
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:03,890
move a lamp closer or further away.

230
00:11:03,890 --> 00:11:05,490
The closer the lamp,

231
00:11:05,490 --> 00:11:07,990
the higher the light intensity.

232
00:11:07,990 --> 00:11:11,530
So, light intensity is
the independent variable:

233
00:11:11,530 --> 00:11:13,340
the one you change.

234
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,950
The rate is the dependent variable:

235
00:11:15,950 --> 00:11:17,810
the one you measure.

236
00:11:17,810 --> 00:11:20,860
And everything else
must be kept constant:

237
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:24,710
the same plant, the same
carbon dioxide concentration,

238
00:11:24,710 --> 00:11:26,270
the same temperature,

239
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:28,370
and no other lights on.

240
00:11:28,370 --> 00:11:30,610
To keep the temperature steady,

241
00:11:30,610 --> 00:11:33,390
stand the beaker in a water bath.

242
00:11:33,390 --> 00:11:34,890
An LED lamp helps,

243
00:11:34,890 --> 00:11:39,330
because it gives off much less
heat than a filament bulb.

244
00:11:39,630 --> 00:11:41,280
At each new distance,

245
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,950
wait a few minutes before you count,

246
00:11:43,950 --> 00:11:46,100
so the plant can adjust.

247
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:49,130
Then repeat, and calculate a mean.

248
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:53,430
You can test the other
two factors the same way.

249
00:11:53,430 --> 00:11:56,160
Just change one thing at a time.

250
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:57,910
To vary carbon dioxide,

251
00:11:57,910 --> 00:12:01,800
use different concentrations
of sodium hydrogencarbonate.

252
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:03,310
To vary temperature,

253
00:12:03,310 --> 00:12:06,790
set the water bath to
different temperatures.

254
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:09,850
Here are the results.

255
00:12:09,850 --> 00:12:11,900
As light intensity increases,

256
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:14,700
the rate of photosynthesis increases.

257
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:16,610
Then it levels off.

258
00:12:16,910 --> 00:12:19,700
Increase the carbon
dioxide concentration,

259
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:21,910
and you get the same shape:

260
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:23,370
the rate increases,

261
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:25,040
then levels off.

262
00:12:25,340 --> 00:12:27,360
Temperature is different.

263
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:30,030
The rate increases up to an optimum,

264
00:12:30,030 --> 00:12:31,750
then falls quickly.

265
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:36,700
That's because the reactions of
photosynthesis are catalysed by enzymes.

266
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:38,110
Below the optimum,

267
00:12:38,110 --> 00:12:42,360
raising the temperature gives the
molecules more kinetic energy,

268
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:47,050
so there are more frequent effective
collisions between enzymes and their

269
00:12:47,050 --> 00:12:49,600
substrates. Above the optimum,

270
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:51,760
the enzymes are denatured.

271
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:54,050
Their active sites change shape,

272
00:12:54,050 --> 00:12:56,790
so the substrates no longer fit.

273
00:12:57,290 --> 00:13:00,060
When a question says
describe a graph,

274
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:03,800
say what happens, and quote
numbers from the axes,

275
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,420
with their units.

276
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:08,250
When it says explain, say why.

277
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,590
Now let's explain those shapes,

278
00:13:11,590 --> 00:13:13,810
using limiting factors.

279
00:13:13,810 --> 00:13:18,720
A limiting factor is something in
short supply that limits the rate of a

280
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:19,810
process.

281
00:13:20,310 --> 00:13:22,460
Back to the light graph.

282
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:24,060
On this rising part,

283
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:27,590
the rate increases as
light intensity increases.

284
00:13:27,590 --> 00:13:30,820
So light intensity is
the limiting factor.

285
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:32,320
On this flat part,

286
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:34,820
more light makes no difference.

287
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:38,490
Light intensity is no
longer the limiting factor.

288
00:13:38,490 --> 00:13:39,900
Something else is,

289
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:43,730
like carbon dioxide
concentration, or temperature.

290
00:13:44,230 --> 00:13:48,980
Now repeat the experiment at a
higher carbon dioxide concentration.

291
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:50,730
At low light intensity,

292
00:13:50,730 --> 00:13:52,910
the two curves are the same,

293
00:13:52,910 --> 00:13:56,780
because light intensity is
still the limiting factor.

294
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:59,840
But the new curve keeps
rising for longer,

295
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,800
and levels off higher.

296
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:06,830
That shows carbon dioxide was the
limiting factor on the flat part.

297
00:14:07,330 --> 00:14:10,290
In the exam, name
the limiting factor,

298
00:14:10,290 --> 00:14:11,970
and give the reason:

299
00:14:11,970 --> 00:14:14,670
increasing it increases the rate.

300
00:14:15,170 --> 00:14:18,860
Different conditions have
different limiting factors.

301
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:21,220
At dawn, or on a dull day,

302
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:24,440
light intensity is usually
the limiting factor,

303
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:26,890
because there's not much light.

304
00:14:26,890 --> 00:14:28,680
On a cold winter's day,

305
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:30,550
it's often temperature.

306
00:14:30,550 --> 00:14:33,280
The molecules have
less kinetic energy,

307
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:36,320
so there are fewer
effective collisions.

308
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:39,080
And on a bright, warm summer's day,

309
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,560
there's plenty of light and warmth,

310
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:44,700
so it's often carbon
dioxide concentration.

311
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:49,040
There's only a tiny amount of
carbon dioxide in the air.

312
00:14:50,190 --> 00:14:52,210
One more practical.

313
00:14:52,210 --> 00:14:56,410
Hydrogencarbonate indicator shows
how much carbon dioxide is in a

314
00:14:56,410 --> 00:15:01,830
solution. At the normal level of
carbon dioxide in air, it's red.

315
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:03,680
With more carbon dioxide,

316
00:15:03,680 --> 00:15:05,250
it turns yellow.

317
00:15:05,250 --> 00:15:07,100
With less carbon dioxide,

318
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:08,770
it turns purple.

319
00:15:09,270 --> 00:15:12,010
Here are three tubes of indicator.

320
00:15:12,010 --> 00:15:13,860
They're sealed with bungs,

321
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:18,040
so no carbon dioxide from
the air can get in or out.

322
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:20,970
One has pondweed, in bright light.

323
00:15:20,970 --> 00:15:22,620
One has pondweed too,

324
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:25,090
but its tube is wrapped in foil,

325
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:26,900
so it's dark inside.

326
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:29,880
And one has no pondweed at all.

327
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:32,160
What colour will each tube be,

328
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:34,020
after a few hours?

329
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:38,040
Pause the video, and
make your prediction.

330
00:15:42,390 --> 00:15:44,410
Here's what happens.

331
00:15:44,410 --> 00:15:47,780
In the light, the
indicator turns purple.

332
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:50,570
Photosynthesis is faster
than respiration,

333
00:15:50,570 --> 00:15:55,400
so the pondweed takes in more
carbon dioxide than it gives out.

334
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:58,380
In the dark, it turns yellow.

335
00:15:58,380 --> 00:16:00,140
There's no photosynthesis,

336
00:16:00,140 --> 00:16:02,090
but respiration carries on,

337
00:16:02,090 --> 00:16:05,370
so the pondweed gives
out carbon dioxide.

338
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:08,600
The tube with no pondweed stays red.

339
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,270
That's the control.

340
00:16:10,270 --> 00:16:14,330
It shows that the pondweed
caused the colour changes.

341
00:16:14,630 --> 00:16:18,470
And in dim light, the
two rates can be equal.

342
00:16:18,470 --> 00:16:22,360
Then there's no net uptake or
release of carbon dioxide,

343
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:24,760
so the indicator stays red.

344
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:27,380
Which busts a classic myth:

345
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:30,120
that plants only respire at night.

346
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:32,210
Plants respire all the time,

347
00:16:32,210 --> 00:16:34,890
day and night, just like you.

348
00:16:34,890 --> 00:16:38,300
In bright light,
photosynthesis is just faster,

349
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:41,570
so there's a net uptake
of carbon dioxide.

350
00:16:41,570 --> 00:16:43,060
Net means overall:

351
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:47,400
the plant takes in more carbon
dioxide than it gives out.

352
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:50,380
Net is the word examiners look for.

353
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:54,360
So, back to van Helmont's willow.

354
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:57,990
Where did those seventy-four
kilograms come from?

355
00:16:58,390 --> 00:17:00,720
Carbon dioxide, from the air,

356
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:03,110
and water, from the soil.

357
00:17:03,110 --> 00:17:04,620
Joined into glucose,

358
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:06,420
using energy from light,

359
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:08,320
then built into cellulose,

360
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:10,190
starch and proteins.

361
00:17:10,490 --> 00:17:14,330
The little that the soil lost
was mostly mineral ions,

362
00:17:14,330 --> 00:17:16,640
like nitrate and magnesium.

363
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:20,700
Van Helmont thought his
tree was made of water.

364
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:22,900
He was only partly right.

365
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:25,580
A living tree is full of water.

366
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:29,710
But most of the wood itself
was built from carbon dioxide,

367
00:17:29,710 --> 00:17:31,860
taken out of thin air.

368
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,540
Let's recap.

369
00:17:34,540 --> 00:17:39,260
Photosynthesis: carbon dioxide plus
water gives glucose plus oxygen,

370
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:42,440
in the presence of
light and chlorophyll.

371
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:47,000
Chlorophyll transfers energy from
light into energy in chemicals.

372
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,290
Glucose is used for respiration,

373
00:17:49,290 --> 00:17:50,800
starch, cellulose,

374
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:52,520
sucrose and nectar.

375
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:55,940
Nitrate ions are needed
to make amino acids.

376
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:59,370
Magnesium ions are needed
to make chlorophyll.

377
00:17:59,370 --> 00:18:01,310
Leaves are broad, thin,

378
00:18:01,310 --> 00:18:02,910
and built in layers,

379
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:05,370
each adapted for photosynthesis.

380
00:18:05,370 --> 00:18:10,110
Light intensity, carbon dioxide
concentration and temperature can all be

381
00:18:10,110 --> 00:18:11,740
limiting factors.

382
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:14,500
And that's plant nutrition.
